<title>ISRAEL: Bank of Israel key lending rate steady for August.</title>
<headline>Bank of Israel key lending rate steady for August.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Israel said on Monday it would leave its key lending rate for August unchanged at an annual 12.7 percent.</p>
<p>The rate is the one charged to commercial banks at daily and weekly tenders.</p>
<p>In mid-June, the central bank cut its base rate by 1.2 percentage points.</p>
</text>
